FOR THESE REASONS, THE COURT UNANIMOUSLY

1.  Holds that in the event of the decision to deport the applicant to Iran being implemented, there would be a violation of Article 3 of Convention;

2.  Holds that there has been a breach of Article 13 of the Convention;

3.  Holds that the finding of a potential breach of Article 3 of the Convention and an actual breach of Article 13 of the Convention constitutes in itself sufficient just satisfaction for any non-pecuniary damage sustained by the applicant;

4.  Dismisses the remainder of the applicant’s claims for just satisfaction.

